{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jethro heard.</b> Note that 'hearing' is used of something not yet present at the time of the narrative. For something already present, 'seeing' applies to both far and near, as in וַיַּרְא יַעֲקֹב כִּי יֶשׁ־שֶׁבֶר בְּמִצְרָיִם (Genesis 42:1), וַיַּרְא בָּלָק (Numbers 22:2), וְרָאוּ כָּל־עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ (Deuteronomy 28:10). And since Israel's exodus from Egypt was already present then, the Sages, of blessed memory, said: What report did he hear? The splitting of the Sea of Reeds and the war with Amalek — because these two had already occurred. However, when we interpret <b>that He brought out</b> as meaning 'when He brought out,' it means he heard all that the blessed Elohim did when He brought Israel out of Egypt — namely the great plagues, the signs and wonders, etc. Therefore his heart was moved to go himself to the wilderness and not to send an agent to Moses with his wife and sons, for he desired to inquire of Elohim — like the king of Babylon who sent to see the sign that was in the land (II Chronicles 32:31)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:03.011837827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}